            <ArticleTitle>[Circumflex coronary artery fistula during staphylococcal aortic valve endocarditis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>592-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We presented a very rare case of the fistula to coronary artery during staphylococcal aortic valve endocarditis in a young man. The tranesophageal echocardiography detected vegetation on aortic valve leaflets and large regurgitatin. During transesophageal echocardiography the peri-anular multi-chamber abscess formation and fistulous communication to circumflex coronary artery was detected.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
